Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1789905599999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789862399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The window high 2771.00 (1787270400000) is 25 bars old and untouched; price is still below the 2680.00 range high on a closing basis, so the breakout leg remains an attempt inside the range, not accepted structure.", "The last bar was rejected at 2700.00, leaving an upper tail of about 67 points, and the prior 2680.00 attempt (1789084800000) closed roughly 165 points below its high; the same zone has produced two visible sellers' reactions, an incipient double top.", "1789430400000 is a wide bear bar (open 2513.91, low 2358.62, close 2397.10) that erased several bull closes in one bar, showing two-sided trade with bears still able to produce strong bars inside the range.", "A 29-bar overlapping range after a near-vertical spike is equally consistent with a climactic spike followed by distribution; the spike's 2771.00 tail bar closed only at 2515.30, well below its high."], "evidence_for": ["The most recent close 2632.98 is the highest close of the supplied 120 bars, and the last two bars are consecutive bull bars that take out the prior six bars' highs and the 2557.46 inner ceiling.", "Whole-window structure is a bull sequence of higher swing lows (1368.42 -> 1512.91 -> 1551.60 -> 1694.74 -> 2357.18) with the 2358.62 low (1789430400000) holding above 2357.18, so the 29-bar sideways stretch follows a strong bull spike and reads as a bull flag rather than a completed top.", "Range pullbacks have been shallow relative to the 1905.63-2771.00 spike: most range closes stay above the spike's midpoint near 2338, and each push down to the 2357-2395 area has been bought back into the 2440-2530 zone.", "Each successive upper test has closed higher (2514.72 at 1789084800000 versus 2632.98 at 1789776000000), i.e. sellers at 2680-2700 have not produced a lower close or an accepted break back down."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed D1 bars, first open 2066.43 (1779494400000), last bar open 2612.03 / high 2700 / low 2604.75 / close 2632.98 (close_time_ms 1789862399999).", "Bars 1-15 of the window decline from high 2143.61 (1779494400000) to low 1368.42 (1780704000000); the 1780704000000 bar has range 1368.42-1599.27 and closes 1568.55 in the upper part of that range with a long lower tail.", "Higher lows follow the 1368.42 low: 1512.91 (1782432000000), 1551.60 (1782777600000), 1694.74 (1783296000000); rising highs reach 1959.37 (1785024000000), then ~12 bars overlap between roughly 1820 and 1960 (1785456000000-1787011200000).", "Three-bar bull spike from 1905.63 to 2771.00: opens/closes 1916.51/2252.16, 2252.20/2326.32, 2326.31/2515.30 at 1787097600000, 1787184000000, 1787270400000; the 2771.00 high leaves a large upper tail on the third bar.", "Since 1787356800000 the market has been sideways: 29 bars between low 2357.18 (1788307200000) and spike highs 2680.00 (1789084800000) and 2700.00 (1789776000000), with most closes between roughly 2390 and 2540 and an inner ceiling at 2557.46 (1787788800000).", "Two separate upside spike attempts above that inner ceiling: 1789084800000 (open 2436.83, high 2680.00, close 2514.72, upper tail ~165) and 1789689600000-1789776000000 (close 2612.02, then high 2700.00 with close 2632.98, upper tail ~67).", "1789430400000 is a large bear bar inside the same range: open 2513.91, low 2358.62, close 2397.10, i.e. a wide body closing near its low.", "The last close 2632.98 is the highest close in the supplied 120-bar window, and the 2700.00 high is still below the window high 2771.00."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening bear leg of the window: 15 bars of lower highs and lower lows from 2143.61 into an accelerating sell-off that reaches 1368.42 (1780704000000), where the bar closes at 1568.55 in the upper 72% of its 1368.42-1599.27 range, a long-lower-tail reversal bar.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779494400000, "upper_boundary": "2143.61"}, {"description": "Recovery and uptrend from the 1368.42 low: higher lows at 1512.91 (1782432000000) and 1551.60 (1782777600000) with rising highs into 1959.37 (1785024000000), followed by an overlapping ~1820-1960 pause (1785456000000-1787011200000) that holds well above the 1368.42 origin.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1959.37"}, {"description": "Three-bar bull spike: bars at 1787097600000, 1787184000000 and 1787270400000 run from 1905.63 to 2771.00 with closes 2252.16, 2326.32 and 2515.30; the 2771.00 extreme is a spike high with a large upper tail and has not been retested.", "end_time_ms": 1787270400000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Trading range after the spike: 29 bars from 1787356800000 to the last bar, bounded by 2357.18 (1788307200000) and the 2680.00 spike high (1789084800000), with heavy overlap, most closes between roughly 2390 and 2540, and an inner ceiling near 2557.46 (1787788800000).", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Two upside spike attempts into the same 2680.00-2700.00 area (1789084800000: high 2680.00, close 2514.72; 1789776000000: high 2700.00, close 2632.98) separated by a sell-off to 2358.62 (1789430400000). The pair is a possible double top at the range high, though the second attempt closes 118 points higher than the first.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789084800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Two-bar bull leg / breakout attempt: 1789689600000 (open 2446.22, high 2643.52, close 2612.02) and 1789776000000 (open 2612.03, high 2700.00, low 2604.75, close 2632.98). Price lifts above the 2557.46 inner ceiling and prints the window's highest close, but has not yet closed above the 2680.00 range high.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Acceptance above the 2680.00 range high, e.g. a close above it followed by another bar closing above 2700.00, would confirm the range breakout and support the bull-trend / breakout-spike read.", "A close back below 2557.46 and into the 2390-2540 range body would negate the breakout attempt and restore an intact trading range between 2357.18 and 2680.00.", "A close below 2357.18 would be a bear breakout from the 29-bar range and would shift the structural read away from the bull flag toward a bear or transition classification.", "Failure to exceed 2680.00 over the next few bars while forming a lower high below 2700.00 would leave the two-sided/double-top interpretation as the strongest alternative and reduce Always-In relevance to low."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789891199999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the last ~27 bars form a clean higher-high/higher-low sequence, and bars 1789732800000 (close 2578.60, range 89.68) and 1789747200000 (close 2636.28) are a strong spike with seven consecutive closes above the prior congestion \u2014 a credible bull breakout with acceptance, i.e. bull-trend/breakout-spike rather than only a range leg.", "The pullback is only two bars and has not tested the 2540.11-2544.63 breakout area (1789401600000) or the 2495.82 spike base, so the breakout is not invalidated; a shallow two-bar pullback after a spike is often a bull flag.", "The equal-low base 2357.18/2358.62 combined with rising highs (2537.57, 2607.62, 2609.02, 2700.00) can be read as an ascending structure rather than a symmetric range."], "evidence_for": ["Range-dominant window: ~40 bars (1788537600000-1789113600000) close within 2436.83-2513.46, and the following 20 bars (1789142400000-1789344000000) hold 2469.28-2609.02, so the majority of the 120 bars are overlapping, two-sided price.", "Repeated failure above 2607-2610: 2607.62 (1789142400000), 2609.02 (1789416000000, close back at 2514.07) and the marginal 2700.00 poke (1789804800000) did not hold; the window closes at 2576.90, below 2609.02 and below the 2618.80 pullback low.", "The 2700.00 high is a one-bar poke whose close sits in the lower quarter of its 77.33 range, followed by two bear bars (1789862400000 low 2569.80; 1789876800000 low 2570.00) that broke the 2608.83 floor of the seven-bar range, so the breakout has no follow-through.", "The pullback already broke below 2578.44, the low of the second spike bar (1789747200000), the first measurable sign of breakout weakness after the spike.", "The equal-low base 2357.18 (1788336000000)/2358.62 (1789488000000) has held twice, consistent with a broad range rather than a one-way trend."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window: 120 closed H4 bars from 1788163200000 to 1789891199999; first close 2445.00, last close 2576.90; whole-window extremes low 2357.18 (1788336000000) and high 2700.00 (1789804800000).", "Mid-window congestion: about 40 bars (1788537600000-1789113600000) overlap heavily with closes 2436.83-2513.46 inside a 2411.04-2528.80 envelope.", "Spike-and-failure bar 1789128000000: open 2457.12, low 2444.19, high 2680.00, close 2555.52; range 235.81 with a 124.48 upper tail.", "Post-spike range 1789142400000-1789344000000 holds 2469.28-2609.02; the push to 2609.02 (1789416000000) closed back at 2514.07 near the bar low.", "Bear leg 1789416000000-1789488000000 falls from 2609.02 to 2358.62, retracing the prior advance back to its base.", "Bull leg 1789488000000-1789804800000 rises 2358.62 to 2700.00 with higher lows 2381.00, 2389.13, 2413.82, 2436.87, 2495.82, 2578.44, 2618.80.", "Breakout bars 1789732800000 (2507.15/2585.50, close 2578.60) and 1789747200000 (2578.44/2643.52, close 2636.28) hold closes above the prior congestion for seven bars.", "Bar 1789804800000 pokes 2700.00 above the 2680.00 and 2609.02 highs but closes 2638.49 in the lower quarter of its 77.33 range.", "Last two bars are bear bars: 1789862400000 (open 2632.98, low 2569.80, close 2586.68) and 1789876800000 (open 2586.68, low 2570.00, close 2576.90); they broke the 2608.83 floor of the seven-bar range and left a 2569.80/2570.00 two-bar shelf.", "The pullback low 2569.80 has broken the 2578.44 low of the second spike bar (1789747200000) but remains above the 2540.11-2544.63 breakout area (1789401600000) and the 2495.82 spike base."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "trading-range", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Window-envelope trading range: the 120 supplied bars sweep 2357.18 to 2700.00 with repeated returns to the 2440-2545 congestion; the extreme lows 2357.18 (1788336000000) and 2358.62 (1789488000000) form a wide equal-low base, and pushes above 2607-2610 (2607.62 at 1789142400000; 2609.02 at 1789416000000) have not held.", "end_time_ms": 1789891199999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1788163200000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Bull leg of the last ~27 bars: successive higher lows 2381.00, 2389.13, 2413.82, 2436.87, 2495.82, 2578.44, 2618.80 off the 2358.62 low (1789488000000), ending in a two-bar spike (1789732800000 close 2578.60; 1789747200000 close 2636.28) and a marginal 2700.00 high (1789804800000). The numeric boundaries are the leg's exact extreme low/high, not a horizontal channel line.", "end_time_ms": 1789891199999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Post-spike seven-bar range 2608.83-2700.00 (1789761600000-1789848000000) built above the prior congestion; the 2700.00 poke (1789804800000) was marginal and the 2608.83 floor was broken by the two bear bars 1789862400000 (close 2586.68) and 1789876800000 (close 2576.90).", "end_time_ms": 1789891199999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2608.83", "start_time_ms": 1789761600000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Possible MTR-like candidate only, at the top of the range: the marginal 2700.00 high (1789804800000, close 2638.49 in the lower quarter of a 77.33 range) sits just above the 2680.00 (1789128000000) and 2609.02 (1789416000000) highs and was followed by two bear bars breaking the 2608.83 range floor. A lower high below 2700.00 plus acceptance below 2569.80 would be needed to develop the pattern; no reversal is established.", "end_time_ms": 1789891199999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1789804800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull confirmation: closes above 2700.00 with a higher low held above 2608.83 would move the read toward bull-trend / breakout-spike.", "Failed-breakout rotation: a lower high below 2700.00 followed by acceptance below 2569.80 and then 2540.11-2544.63 would confirm the failed breakout and shift the read toward a bear leg inside the range.", "Bull-flag resolution: a bull reversal bar closing back above 2608.83-2618.80 would classify the two-bar pullback as a bull flag within the bull leg.", "Range continuation: renewed overlapping bars inside 2440.00-2545.00 with the 2357.18-2358.62 base untested keeps the trading-range/range read.", "Range breakdown: closes below 2357.18 would open a bear-tren